    "leakage_mechanism_identified_in_candidate_v2": {
      "severity": "CRITICAL_METHODOLOGICAL_LEAKAGE",
      "description": "In Candidate RF v2, synthetic training samples were filtered by parent spatial fold != k, which prevented direct row leakage. However, their pseudo-labels (teacher_prediction) were generated by a global teacher model that had been fitted on all 838 records, including the held-out validation fold k records. This allowed subtle decision-boundary information from validation fold k to leak into the training partition via the teacher's predictions.",
      "remedy": "To achieve 100% leak-free spatial evaluation, a separate teacher model must be trained inside each fold using ONLY that fold's training partition (Candidate 4 [spatial_fold != k]). This fold-isolated teacher then predicts pseudo-labels strictly for training-fold synthetic records."
    }
  },
